# Destin8 Admin Panel - Full Feature Implementation Plan

## Overview
The Admin Panel serves as the nerve center for the Destin8 platform. It enables platform administrators to govern agencies, moderate content, and manage all users. The panel is web-based (React + Vite) and connects to the FastAPI backend.

---

## Pages & Features

### Page 1: Analytics Dashboard (Home Screen)
A high-level overview of platform health, shown immediately after login.

**Cards/Metrics:**
- Total Travelers registered
- Total Agencies (split by: Pending / Approved / Rejected)
- Total Travel Packages posted
- New registrations in the last 7 days

**Implementation:**
- **Backend:** `GET /api/admin/stats` — returns all aggregate counts via a single efficient query.
- **Frontend:** `AnalyticsScreen.jsx` with stat cards and clean data layout using the Destin8 Design System.

---

### Page 2: Agency Approvals *(Already Built — Needs Minor Enhancements)*
Review and approve/reject travel agency registrations.

**Enhancements to existing screen:**
- Show **rejection reason** on rejected agency cards.
- Add a **details expandable row** showing full business address and license number.
- Filter tabs: Pending / Approved / Rejected / All.

---

### Page 3: User Directory
A searchable, filterable list of ALL users on the platform (Travelers, Agencies, Admins).

**Features:**
- Table columns: Name, Email, Role, Status, Date Joined.
- Filter by role: All / Traveler / Agency / Admin.
- **Suspend/Activate** toggle: Instantly block or restore a user's access without deleting their data.
- **Create Admin Account** button: Opens a modal to add a new admin/staff account with name, email, and password. Only creates `admin` role accounts — Travelers/Agencies register via the mobile app.
- **View Details** panel: Click a user to see a side panel with their full info (read-only). For agencies, this links to their profile.

**Backend:**
- `GET /api/admin/users?role=traveler|agency|admin` — Fetch all users, filtered by role.
- `PUT /api/admin/users/{user_id}/suspend` — Sets `status` to `suspended`.
- `PUT /api/admin/users/{user_id}/activate` — Sets `status` back to `active`.
- `POST /api/admin/users` — Create a new admin account (role locked to `admin`).

**Note on Password/Email Editing:** Admins do **not** directly edit user passwords or emails. If a user reports a login issue, the proper solution is account suspension + directing them to a support channel. This follows security best practices.

---

### Page 4: Package Moderation *(Relevant after Week 2 - Packages are built)*
Once agencies can post Travel Packages, this screen allows the admin to oversee all content.

**Features:**
- Table: Package Title, Agency Name, Price, Duration, Status (Active / Taken Down).
- **Take Down** button: Marks a package as inactive/hidden so travelers can't see it.
- **Restore** button: Re-activates a taken-down package.
- View package details in an expandable row.

**Backend:**
- `GET /api/admin/packages` — Fetch all packages across all agencies.
- `PUT /api/admin/packages/{package_id}/takedown`
- `PUT /api/admin/packages/{package_id}/restore`

> [!NOTE]
> This page will be built **alongside** the Package CRUD feature in Week 2. It is listed here for completeness.

